\begin_layout Paragraph
Shape Update
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
An agent 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{A}_{i}$
\end_inset

 can update its shape by updating the bounds of its associated orthotope 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{H}_{i}^{t}$
\end_inset

 at learning step 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

 by a factor 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha$
\end_inset

 in the direction of an input 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

.
 The factor 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha$
\end_inset

 is a hyperparameter that needs to be tuned.
 The bounds of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{H}_{i}^{t}$
\end_inset

 are updated to obtain 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{H}_{i}^{t+1}$
\end_inset

 according to the following relationship
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align}
h_{j}^{t+1} & =\begin{cases}
\left(h_{i,j}^{t}-l_{j}^{t}\right)\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{n}}+l_{j}^{t} & \text{if }l_{i,j}^{t}\leq x_{j}\leq h_{i,j}^{t}\\
h_{i,j}^{t} & \text{else}
\end{cases}\\
l_{j}^{t+1} & =\begin{cases}
\left(l_{i,j}^{t}-h_{i,j}^{t}\right)\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{n}}+h_{j}^{t} & \text{if }l_{i,j}^{t}\leq x_{j}\leq h_{i,j}^{t}\\
l_{i,j}^{t} & \text{else}
\end{cases}
\end{align}

\end_inset

with 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
\varepsilon=\begin{cases}
\left(1+\alpha\right) & \text{if expansion}\\
\left(1-\alpha\right) & \text{if retraction}
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

\end_inset

and 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

 the number of features such that 
\begin_inset Formula $l_{i,j}^{t}\leq x_{j}\leq h_{i,j}^{t}$
\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus,
 the new volume of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{H}_{i}$
\end_inset

 is given by the relation:
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align}
V\left(\mathcal{H}_{i}^{t+1}\right) & =\varepsilon V\left(\mathcal{H}_{i}^{t}\right)
\end{align}

\end_inset

The mechanism of expansion consists in expanding the boundaries of the area of expertise defined by the activation function of the agent,
 as illustrated in Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:Expansion-oCELL"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

.
 Conversely,
 the mechanism shrinks these boundaries,
 as shown in Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:Retraction-oCELL"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

