\begin_layout Plain Layout
GPs do not scale well => in this work we propose horizontal scaling by using GPs inside the local expert agents => many small GPs instead of one big GP
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Challenging to design a system with GPs as they are not inherently online learning models/
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
same spatialization as kCELL with RBF kernels for activation functions 
\begin_inset Formula $\phi_{i}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
use of GP as internal models 
\begin_inset Formula $f_{i}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
in 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{\mathcal{M}}_{i}$
\end_inset

 => stores confidence value 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{C}_{\mathcal{A}_{i}}$
\end_inset

 and a memory of points used to build the internal GP model (X_train and y_train)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Gating mechanism works the same as for kCELL.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
UPDATE MODEL:
 Models updated by chosing to ignore the 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{new}$
\end_inset

,
 to swap 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{new}$
\end_inset

 with a point of the memory or to add 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{new}$
\end_inset

 to the memory.
 For this it evaluates the cost of each configuration:
 nominal (ignore 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{new}$
\end_inset

),
 swap with a given point 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{i}$
\end_inset

 from the memory,
 add to the memory.
 Then the action that leads to the minimal cost is chosen.
 => the cost function used to evaluate the configurations is the AIC (Akaike Information Criterion) with the log likelihood associated with the configuration and the number of points in memory as the number of parameters.
 => This way each local expert agent handles its own memory following a tradeoff between complexity and accuracy => to summarize,
 each local expert agent performs a model selection at each update step
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
UPDATE SHAPE:
 mixed with UPDATE MODEL as the shape is determined by the covariance and mean of X_train
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Prediction Mean and Var:
 The global prediction corresponds to the prediction of the most confident GP,
 i.e the agent that predicts the minimum uncertainty on its prediction.
 => because gaussian processes are strong inside their area of expertise but outside they can be very weak => that's why we chose the closest.
\end_layout

