\begin_layout Paragraph
Uncertainty Quantification Analysis
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
One of the main advantage of the use of GPs in gpCELL is the ability to provide 
\series bold
predictive variance measurement
\series default
.
 This is complementary with the epistemic uncertainty estimation derived from the spatialization of local expert agents.
 Despite the ability of GPs to provide a well-calibrated uncertainty estimates,
 the calibration of predictive uncertainty in the ensemble of local expert agents in gpCELL is not mathematically guaranteed,
 and should be verified experimentally.
 To this end,
 the Prediction Interval Coverage Probability (PICP) is measured on the test set.
 PICP represents the proportion of true observations that fall inside the predicted 95% confidence interval.
 As shown in Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:gpCELL-PICP"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

,
 the PICP exceeds 0.95 for every output dimension.
 This result demonstrates that gpCELL provides 
\series bold
well-calibrated intervals
\series default
.
 It means that the true torque values fall within the predicted 95% confidence range with high reliability.
\end_layout

