\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Architecture diagram of the proposed architecture for speed recommendation.
 The 
\emph on
Speed Recommendation System
\emph default
 follows a MPC architecture.
 It includes the 
\emph on
optimizer
\emph default
 that exploits the predictions from a 
\emph on
CELL predictive model 
\emph default
to obtain the optimal speed recommendation 
\begin_inset Formula $v_{t}^{*}$
\end_inset

 from an initial state 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{t}$
\end_inset

.
 The speed recommendation setpoint 
\begin_inset Formula $v_{t}^{*}$
\end_inset

 is then transmitted to the 
\emph on
driver
\emph default
 who acts on the vehicle through gear shifts,
 the brake and accelerator pedal.
 The initial state 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{t}$
\end_inset

 is built from the state of the vehicle 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{\text{vehicle}}$
\end_inset

 and from the driving context 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{\text{context}}$
\end_inset

 such as 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{t}=\left[s_{\text{context}},\,s_{\text{vehicle}}\right]$
\end_inset

.
 The 
\emph on
CELL predictive model
\emph default
 is continuously learning from the successive states.
